index 00000000..0b1d9816
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FIX_SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Fix for device_init() Error Return Value Issue
+
+## Problem
+When `device_init()` is called on a deferred device whose initialization function returns an error, the call was returning the positive errno value instead of the negative one. This violated the convention that failing initialization should return -errno.
+
+## Root Cause
+In `kernel/init.c`, the `do_device_init()` function was incorrectly negating negative error codes:
+```c
+if (rc < 0) {
+    rc = -rc;  // This converted -EIO to EIO
+}
+```
+
+This meant:
+- If init returned -EIO, device_init() returned EIO (wrong!)
+- If init returned EIO, device_init() returned EIO (wrong!)
+
+## Solution
+Modified `do_device_init()` in `kernel/init.c` to:
+1. Store the absolute value (positive errno) in `dev->state->init_res` for device state tracking
+2. Return negative error codes to the caller (converting positive errors to negative)
+
+The fix ensures:
+- `device_init()` always returns negative error codes (e.g., -EIO)
+- `dev->state->init_res` stores positive errno values (as expected by `device_is_ready()`)
+- Both positive and negative error returns from init functions are handled correctly
+
+## Changes Made
+File: `kernel/init.c`
+- Lines 319-327: Replaced error handling logic to store absolute value in init_res
+- Lines 329-333: Added logic to convert positive error codes to negative before returning
+
+## Testing
+All existing kernel device tests pass with this fix:
+- `tests/kernel/device` - All tests passed
+- `tests/kernel/common` - All tests passed
+
+The fix correctly handles:
+1. Init functions returning positive errors (e.g., EIO) → device_init() returns -EIO
+2. Init functions returning negative errors (e.g., -EIO) → device_init() returns -EIO
+3. Successful initialization (0) → device_init() returns 0
+4. Repeated initialization → device_init() returns -EALREADY
diff --git a/kernel/init.c b/kernel/init.c
index dd9f3d72..5438217d 100644
--- a/kernel/init.c
+++ b/kernel/init.c
@@ -317,13 +317,17 @@ static int do_device_init(const struct device *dev)
 		 * failed, record the error condition.
 		 */
 		if (rc != 0) {
-			if (rc < 0) {
-				rc = -rc;
-			}
+			/* Store the absolute value of the error code */
+			int abs_rc = rc < 0 ? -rc : rc;
 			if (rc > UINT8_MAX) {
-				rc = UINT8_MAX;
+				abs_rc = UINT8_MAX;
+			}
+			dev->state->init_res = abs_rc;
+
+			/* Return the error code as negative */
+			if (rc > 0) {
+				rc = -rc;
 			}
-			dev->state->init_res = rc;
 		}
 	}
 
